# The Full Parameter List's grid (the ConfigRawParams remainder, after rows 81 and 82): the
# RawParamWarning box, the columns' widths and the splitter kept in config.xml, the Fav column and
# its sort, the Desc column, the Options column's NumericUpDown, the typed Value cell's
# out-of-range question answered No, and Ctrl+S with nothing to write.
#
# The claims, each the C#'s (GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigRawParams.cs):
# * Activate shows Common.MessageShowAgain(Strings.RawParamWarning, ...) (:92) every time, until
#   its "Show me again?" is unticked, which is saved as SHOWAGAIN_Raw_Param_Warning False
#   (Common.cs:260-270, 446-449).
# * Activate sets each resizable column's width from rawparam_<column>_width and the splitter
#   from rawparam_splitterdistance (:70-84); Deactivate writes them all back (:99-112). This test's
#   config.xml gives the Options column 222 and the splitter 260; the rest are the .resx's.
# * The Fav cell ticked appends the name to fav_params and sorts the grid, favourites first, by
#   name in natural order (:1045-1063, :833-858). Unticking the last favourite calls SetList with
#   an empty list, which returns without touching the setting (ExtLibs/Utilities/Settings.cs:171-
#   176): the cell unticks and fav_params keeps the name.
# * Desc, Units and Options come from the documentation (:604-645). RTL_LOIT_TIME's bundled
#   documentation: "Time (in milliseconds) to loiter above home before beginning final descent",
#   ms, 0 to 60000 in steps of 1000 - so the row entered gets a NumericUpDown (:1270-1316) whose
#   arrows put their text in the Value cell, which is an edit, written here as it is made.
# * A typed value outside the range asks "RTL_LOIT_TIME value is out of range. Do you want to
#   continue?" under "Out of range"; No keeps the old value (:499-516).
# * Ctrl+S is Write Params (:116-125); with nothing waiting it says "No parameters were changed."
#   under "No changes" (:370-371).
#
# NOT RUN HERE: dragging a header's edge or the splitter - the runner has no drag; the drag is
# proven in crates/mp-gui/src/raw_params_grid.rs (a_drag_moves_a_width_and_the_splitter), and
# the widths here are the settings' and the restart's. The ReadOnly box needs the fetched
# apm.pdef.xml's ReadOnly field (an_edit_writes_or_asks); Ctrl+S's writes and the reboot's box
# need a write never echoed (write_params_writes_and_says_a_reboot_is_required).
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, with
# RTL_LOIT_TIME at its default 5000. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/params-list-columns.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
setup printf '\357\273\277<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>\n<Config>\n  <rawparam_Options_width>222</rawparam_Options_width>\n  <rawparam_splitterdistance>260</rawparam_splitterdistance>\n</Config>' > "$WORK/config.xml"

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 23

expect vehicle.connected true
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.active true

# RawParamWarning, "Show me again?" ticked; OK closes it.
expect params.warning true
expect params.config.SHOWAGAIN_Raw_Param_Warning none
click raw-param-warning-ok
expect params.warning false

# The widths and the splitter as config.xml has them; the rest the .resx's.
expect params.width.Options 222
expect params.width.Command 130
expect params.width.Value 70
expect params.width.Units 60
expect params.width.Fav 30
expect params.splitter 260

# RTL's rows in natural order; RTL_LOIT_TIME made a favourite goes first.
# The tree lists every group; RTL lies below a 1200-pixel window: wheeled into view.
reveal params-tree param-group-RTL
click param-group-RTL
expect params.fav none
expect params.rows.first RTL_ALT_FINAL_M
click param-fav-RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.fav RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.config.fav_params RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.rows.first RTL_LOIT_TIME

# A header clicked sorts by its column, and again turns the order round; the favourite stays
# first either way, as OnParamsOnSortCompare keeps it. Name descending puts RTL_ALT_FINAL_M last.
expect params.sort Command asc
click param-col-Command
expect params.sort Command desc
expect params.rows.first RTL_LOIT_TIME
click param-col-Value
expect params.sort Value asc
click param-col-Command
expect params.sort Command asc
expect params.rows.first RTL_LOIT_TIME

# The Fav click entered the row: its documentation, and the NumericUpDown over its range.
expect params.selected.desc ~ loiter above home
expect params.selected.units ms
expect params.selected.options 0 60000
expect params.selected.value 5000
expect params.control range
expect params.control.text 5000

# The typed Value cell: out of range, asked, No - nothing written, the value kept.
expect params.write.name none
doubleclick param-value-RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.editing RTL_LOIT_TIME
key ctrl+u
type 99999
key Return
expect params.editing none
expect params.box Out of range
expect params.box.text RTL_LOIT_TIME value is out of range. Do you want to continue?
click param-box-no
expect params.box none
expect params.write.name none
expect params.selected.value 5000
expect params.red none

# The NumericUpDown's arrows: 6000 written and heard back, then 5000 again.
click param-options-up
expect params.control.text 6000
expect params.write.name RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.write.outcome accepted
expect params.selected.value 6000
expect params.changes 0
click param-options-down
expect params.write.outcome accepted
expect params.selected.value 5000

# Ctrl+S from the grid with nothing waiting.
click param-value-RTL_LOIT_TIME
key ctrl+s
expect params.box No changes
expect params.box.text No parameters were changed.
click param-box-ok
expect params.box none

# Leaving is Deactivate: every width and the splitter into the settings.
click tab-fly
expect params.active false
expect params.config.rawparam_Options_width 222
expect params.config.rawparam_Command_width 130
expect params.config.rawparam_Default_value_width 70
expect params.config.rawparam_Fav_width 30
expect params.config.rawparam_splitterdistance 260

# The close box saves config.xml; the next start reads the widths, the splitter and the favourite.
restart
expect params.active true
expect params.warning true
expect params.width.Options 222
expect params.splitter 260
expect params.fav RTL_LOIT_TIME

# "Show me again?" unticked: saved False, and the next Activate asks nothing.
click raw-param-warning-again
expect params.config.SHOWAGAIN_Raw_Param_Warning False
click raw-param-warning-ok
click tab-fly
click tab-params
expect params.active true
expect params.warning false

# The last favourite unticked: the cell unticks, the setting keeps it (SetList of nothing).
# The tree is drawn afresh on each return to the screen, unscrolled: wheeled to RTL again.
reveal params-tree param-group-RTL
click param-group-RTL
click param-fav-RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.fav none
expect params.config.fav_params RTL_LOIT_TIME
expect params.rows.first RTL_ALT_FINAL_M
